    "text": "Let the shortest distance between the lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mo>:</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>z</mi></math>&nbsp;be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>6</mn></msqrt></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>)</mo></math> lies on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math>, then which of the following is NOT possible?",
